owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:fd620dc380b563ff699c644f38d970b4\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"The selected engagement has the Product-composition scope described by this clause.\"],\"definition\":\"Dependency-ready work needs executable prerequisites; provider replacement preserves material contracts or enters an authorized successor relation.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":979,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-06 — Readiness, cycles and replacement\\n\\nWork selects a dependency-ready frontier at the required subjects and revisions.\\nA cycle in declared Product relationships need not be a cycle in the selected\\nwork. A cycle of current prerequisite claims requires an executable resolution:\\nfor example an admitted prior revision, explicit seed, staged contract or bounded\\niteration with its continuation/stop conditions. Naming a lead alone does not\\nsupply a missing prerequisite or establish convergence.\\n\\nReplacing a constituent or refining it into further Products preserves the\\nconsumer's material contract: meaning, preconditions, effects, failures,\\nauthority, lifecycle, evidence and subsequent obligations. A semantic change\\nrequires an authorized successor relation and affected reassessment. The [ACTIVATION refinement contract](ACTIVATION.md#refinement) governs this\\npreservation. Matching signatures, labels or a sample output is insufficient (P4a, P6). New capabilities may be\\nadded without silently widening existing consumers' duties or grants.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-06--readiness-cycles-and-replacement\",\"start_line\":964}],\"label\":\"Readiness cycles and lawful replacement\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:47baa21d65a4c2545e5bcfe1d5034327","key":18,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:fd620dc380b563ff699c644f38d970b4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:47baa21d65a4c2545e5bcfe1d5034327\",\"judgment_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:judgment-kind:external-semantic-review\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:constraint-kind:authored-source-statement\",\"latitude_ref\":[],\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"predicate\":{\"conditions\":[\"Apply the clause within its explicitly stated scope and qualifications.\"],\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":979,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-06 — Readiness, cycles and replacement\\n\\nWork selects a dependency-ready frontier at the required subjects and revisions.\\nA cycle in declared Product relationships need not be a cycle in the selected\\nwork. A cycle of current prerequisite claims requires an executable resolution:\\nfor example an admitted prior revision, explicit seed, staged contract or bounded\\niteration with its continuation/stop conditions. Naming a lead alone does not\\nsupply a missing prerequisite or establish convergence.\\n\\nReplacing a constituent or refining it into further Products preserves the\\nconsumer's material contract: meaning, preconditions, effects, failures,\\nauthority, lifecycle, evidence and subsequent obligations. A semantic change\\nrequires an authorized successor relation and affected reassessment. The [ACTIVATION refinement contract](ACTIVATION.md#refinement) governs this\\npreservation. Matching signatures, labels or a sample output is insufficient (P4a, P6). New capabilities may be\\nadded without silently widening existing consumers' duties or grants.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-06--readiness-cycles-and-replacement\",\"start_line\":964}],\"statement\":\"Work selects a dependency-ready frontier at the required subjects and revisions.\\nA cycle in declared Product relationships need not be a cycle in the selected\\nwork. A cycle of current prerequisite claims requires an executable resolution:\\nfor example an admitted prior revision, explicit seed, staged contract or bounded\\niteration with its continuation/stop conditions. Naming a lead alone does not\\nsupply a missing prerequisite or establish convergence.\\n\\nReplacing a constituent or refining it into further Products preserves the\\nconsumer's material contract: meaning, preconditions, effects, failures,\\nauthority, lifecycle, evidence and subsequent obligations. A semantic change\\nrequires an authorized successor relation and affected reassessment. The [ACTIVATION refinement contract](ACTIVATION.md#refinement) governs this\\npreservation. Matching signatures, labels or a sample output is insufficient (P4a, P6). New capabilities may be\\nadded without silently widening existing consumers' duties or grants.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:12a722d0655ad76ca2ff85dbb231246e","key":26,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":979,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-06 — Readiness, cycles and replacement\\n\\nWork selects a dependency-ready frontier at the required subjects and revisions.\\nA cycle in declared Product relationships need not be a cycle in the selected\\nwork. A cycle of current prerequisite claims requires an executable resolution:\\nfor example an admitted prior revision, explicit seed, staged contract or bounded\\niteration with its continuation/stop conditions. Naming a lead alone does not\\nsupply a missing prerequisite or establish convergence.\\n\\nReplacing a constituent or refining it into further Products preserves the\\nconsumer's material contract: meaning, preconditions, effects, failures,\\nauthority, lifecycle, evidence and subsequent obligations. A semantic change\\nrequires an authorized successor relation and affected reassessment. The [ACTIVATION refinement contract](ACTIVATION.md#refinement) governs this\\npreservation. Matching signatures, labels or a sample output is insufficient (P4a, P6). New capabilities may be\\nadded without silently widening existing consumers' duties or grants.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-06--readiness-cycles-and-replacement\",\"start_line\":964}],\"statements\":[\"Resolve current prerequisites with a lawful prior revision, explicit seed, staged contract or bounded iteration.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:fd620dc380b563ff699c644f38d970b4\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":979,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-06 — Readiness, cycles and replacement\\n\\nWork selects a dependency-ready frontier at the required subjects and revisions.\\nA cycle in declared Product relationships need not be a cycle in the selected\\nwork. A cycle of current prerequisite claims requires an executable resolution:\\nfor example an admitted prior revision, explicit seed, staged contract or bounded\\niteration with its continuation/stop conditions. Naming a lead alone does not\\nsupply a missing prerequisite or establish convergence.\\n\\nReplacing a constituent or refining it into further Products preserves the\\nconsumer's material contract: meaning, preconditions, effects, failures,\\nauthority, lifecycle, evidence and subsequent obligations. A semantic change\\nrequires an authorized successor relation and affected reassessment. The [ACTIVATION refinement contract](ACTIVATION.md#refinement) governs this\\npreservation. Matching signatures, labels or a sample output is insufficient (P4a, P6). New capabilities may be\\nadded without silently widening existing consumers' duties or grants.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-06--readiness-cycles-and-replacement\",\"start_line\":964}],\"statements\":[\"Treat a named lead as missing evidence or silently change consumer obligations on replacement.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:12a722d0655ad76ca2ff85dbb231246e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"seeds":[5],"unresolved":[]},"underbudgetRefusal":"insufficient record budget; required closure is not truncated"},{"budget":11,"projection":{"excluded":[0,1,3,5,7,8,9,10,13,14,16,18,20,21,22,23,24,25,26,28,31],"excludedResiduals":[{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9","key":31,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the exact evidence and owner verdicts for each semantic or acceptance claim.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6cc92570e9e1d4cc0b93ea894305e162\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Immutable stable publication\\n\\nStable publication applies the same scope, source reconciliation, proportionate\\nchecks, exact carrier, subtree and inventory obligations as RC publication.\\nIt instead creates one stable-v1 annotated tag and any explicitly selected\\nrelease branch, with no RC branch or separate selector. Before publication,\\nverify the fresh-line conditions of [Stable cuts](#stable-cuts), bind remote\\nabsence for the immutable tag and bind every mutable destination's expected\\nobject. Publish the selected refs atomically where supported; a changed\\nexpectation stops publication for reconciliation. Read back the remote tag\\nobject, commit, subtree and declared assets. The release is publicly classified\\nas a normal published release; release-host flags do not replace exact identity\\nor qualification evidence (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#immutable-stable-publication\",\"start_line\":361}],\"statement\":\"A stable naming and discovery profile alone does not establish stronger semantic qualification.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"external":[{"identity":"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record","payload":"{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"evidence_identity\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:evidence:explicit-generation-signature\",\"external_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record\",\"external_target_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:external-kind:source-section\",\"reference_domain\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:reference-domain:declared\",\"resolution_basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"resolved_target_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record\"}"},{"identity":"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions","payload":"{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"evidence_identity\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:evidence:explicit-generation-signature\",\"external_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-roo