 `sync`; it does not\\nexpress that choice through the latest-version channel (P5, P6).\\n\\nFor a stable line, channel resolution returns its verified stable-v1 cut\\nwithout ordinal comparison or a separate selector. A legacy bare selector is\\nnever admitted as a stable exact basis; an ambiguous profile is refused. The\\nsame digest-bound adoption operation applies to either profile (P3, P5, P6).\\n\\nPresentation and mutation are separate invocations. The read-only plan,\\nthe Adoption Plan of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4, binds the current Product\\nDefinition bytes and basis to the target immutable cut, annotated tag\\nobject, peeled commit, tree and installed-manifest digest, then emits a\\ndeterministic plan digest. Mutation requires that exact digest as the\\noperator's acceptance and re-derives it before changing any Product\\nDefinition. Selector, target, manifest or definition drift invalidates the\\nacceptance. A fleet uses the same law with one aggregate digest over all\\nexact per-definition plans. Planning inside a mutating invocation is not\\nexternal presentation and cannot authorise itself. The plan's hashing rule\\nand the manager's command boundaries are PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4 (P6, P3).\\n\\nThis split lets operators refer to `v<version>` for the latest published\\nRC without repeatedly incrementing the version line, while every governed\\nproject retains reproducible exact-cut authority and changes only through\\nexplicit adoption (P2, P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#4-selector-and-consumer-adoption\",\"start_line\":428}],\"statement\":\"An RC-profile version-line selector answers only (P6, P3):\\n\\n> Which highest-ordinal published immutable RC cut currently exists on\\n> this version line?\\n\\nIt never answers:\\n\\n> Which exact STDO cut governs this consumer?\\n\\nA Product Definition may retain `stdo://channels/<version>` as its\\ndiscovery selector, but its operative basis is the exact\\n`stdo://releases/v<version>-rc.<n>/` or stable\\n`stdo://releases/v<major>.<minor>.<patch>/` URI and installed-manifest digest,\\nthe installed release basis of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4. Moving the Git\\nversion-line selector does not update any consumer. Adoption is a separate\\nexplicit Product-Definition transition that resolves, presents, installs,\\nverifies and pins the selected immutable cut. RC resolution requires an\\nannotated selector with a distinct peeled commit; absence of a peeled\\nselector ref fails closed and cannot be interpreted as a lightweight\\nselector whose tag object is its commit (P6, P3, P5).\\n\\nFor an RC line, channel resolution enumerates the published RC tags for the selected\\nProject Release Namespace, including preserved unqualified historical cuts\\nduring a namespace transition, selects the greatest positive ordinal,\\nrequires that cut and the current selector to be annotated tags peeling to\\nthe same commit, and fails closed when the selector lags or points\\nelsewhere. Channel adoption also refuses a same-line target whose ordinal\\nis below the Product Definition's current exact basis. A consumer that\\nintentionally retains an older cut names that immutable RC URI and digest\\nexplicitly and uses exact-basis operations such as `sync`; it does not\\nexpress that choice through the latest-version channel (P5, P6).\\n\\nFor a stable line, channel resolution returns its verified stable-v1 cut\\nwithout ordinal comparison or a separate selector. A legacy bare selector is\\nnever admitted as a stable exact basis; an ambiguous profile is refused. The\\nsame digest-bound adoption operation applies to either profile (P3, P5, P6).\\n\\nPresentation and mutation are separate invocations. The read-only plan,\\nthe Adoption Plan of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4, binds the current Product\\nDefinition bytes and basis to the target immutable cut, annotated tag\\nobject, peeled commit, tree and installed-manifest digest, then emits a\\ndeterministic plan digest. Mutation requires that exact digest as the\\noperator's acceptance and re-derives it before changing any Product\\nDefinition. Selector, target, manifest or definition drift invalidates the\\nacceptance. A fleet uses the same law with one aggregate digest over all\\nexact per-definition plans. Planning inside a mutating invocation is not\\nexternal presentation and cannot authorise itself. The plan's hashing rule\\nand the manager's command boundaries are PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4 (P6, P3).\\n\\nThis split lets operators refer to `v<version>` for the latest published\\nRC without repeatedly incrementing the version line, while every governed\\nproject retains reproducible exact-cut authority and changes only through\\nexplicit adoption (P2, P3, P6).\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"seeds":[9],"unresolved":[]},"underbudgetRefusal":"insufficient record budget; required closure is not truncated"},{"budget":6,"projection":{"excluded":[0,1,4,5,6,7,8,9,11,12,13,14,17,18,19,20,21,22,23,24,26,27,28,29,30,31],"excludedResiduals":[{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3","key":29,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep unsupported adequacy/clean-room claims unresolved and use the declared re-entry.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:acc8c965a48d0a6498144ae726e9a1a5\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":963,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-05 — Context construction and clean-room conditions\\n\\nAn actor's selected context must satisfy both permission and adequacy for its\\nengagement. Permission covers the source information and permitted derivations,\\nnot only paths or filenames. The boundary identifies eligible source classes,\\nexports and tool outputs, material provenance, intended use, later acquisitions\\nand the effect of prior exposure. An allowed file location or a fresh summary\\ndoes not sanitize prohibited information.\\n\\nA target owner may authorize an export, but clean-room eligibility additionally\\nrequires that the engagement's information policy admits that export and its\\nprovenance. The actual delivered/acquired material must be recorded to the extent\\nrequired by the claim. An uncertain or prohibited exposure follows the declared\\nhold/re-entry rule; it cannot be repaired by deleting its receipt or relabeling\\nthe same actor fresh. Prior actor knowledge and external acquisition channels are\\npart of the declared limits.\\n\\nAdequacy retains the distinctions required for the task's decisions and\\ncontinuations, including unresolved obligations, result standing, currentness and\\nauthority. If the permitted material is insufficient, acquire an authorized\\nextension, narrow the task with the owner, use a suitable actor or return the\\nunresolved outcome. Permission is not evidence of sufficiency, and a budget is\\nnot permission to omit a deciding condition. This applies [FOUNDATIONS Observation sufficiency](FOUNDATIONS.md#assurance-relations)\\nand its scoped preservation law; it supplies no general optimal context selector (P1, P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions\",\"start_line\":939}],\"statement\":\"Permission alone cannot establish semantic sufficiency or exclude unknown prior/external exposure.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:a62977ad70d316938830d82d18f33f6d","key":30,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Hold dependent assurance or widen assessment without erasing original evidence.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:a62977ad70d316938830d82d18f33f6d\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:759dcede800bb40bf1b35ef8393b00f2\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":995,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-07 — Change, evidence and reliance\\n\\nEach cross-boundary use binds the actual selected sources and material execution\\nbasis, including uncommitted bytes where relevant. A moving selection identifies\\nhow advancement is detected and which reliance must be reassessed. Git is one\\npossible carrier, not a mandatory identity system.\\n\\nChanges and new counterexamples propagate through material assertion, execution\\nand evidence-use dependencies under [FOUNDATIONS Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse). Historical\\nevidence remains about its original subject. Reuse on a changed subject needs an\\nestablished applicability or preservation relation; rereading alone does not\\nestablish it. A new release does not invalidate a still-selected older release,\\nand a changed hash alone establishes neither semantic incompatibility nor\\ncontinued validity. Unknown impact holds the dependent assurance or widens\\nassessment; it does not require unrelated work to restart.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-07--change-evidence-and-reliance\",\"start_line\":980}],\"statement\":\"Material impact may remain unknown after a change.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9","key":31,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the exact evidence and owner verdicts for each semantic or acceptance claim.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6cc92570e9e1d4cc0b93ea894305e162\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Immutable stable publication\\n\\nStable publication applies the same scope, source reconciliation, proportionate\\nchecks, exact carrier, subtree and inventory obligations as RC publication.\\nIt instead creates one stable-v1 annotated tag and any explicitly selected\\nrelease branch, with no RC branch or separate selector. Before publication,\\nverify the fresh-line conditions of [Stable cuts](#stable-cuts), bind remote\\nabsence for the immutable tag and bind every mutable destination's expected\\nobject. Publish the selected refs atomically where supported; a changed\\nexpectation stops publication for reconciliation. Read back the remote tag\\nobject, commit, subtree and declared assets. The release is publicly classified\\nas a normal published release; release-host flags do not replace exact identity\\nor qualification evidence (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#immutable-stable-publication\",\"start_line\":361}],\"statement\":\"A stable naming and discovery profile alone does not establish stronger semantic qualification.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"external":[{"identity":"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record","payload":"{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"evidence_identity\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:evidence:explicit-generation-signature\",\"external_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT