s not\\nestablish it. A new release does not invalidate a still-selected older release,\\nand a changed hash alone establishes neither semantic incompatibility nor\\ncontinued validity. Unknown impact holds the dependent assurance or widens\\nassessment; it does not require unrelated work to restart.\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3e3f03245d00d6080a6a206cef4a155e","key":27,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":995,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-07 — Change, evidence and reliance\\n\\nEach cross-boundary use binds the actual selected sources and material execution\\nbasis, including uncommitted bytes where relevant. A moving selection identifies\\nhow advancement is detected and which reliance must be reassessed. Git is one\\npossible carrier, not a mandatory identity system.\\n\\nChanges and new counterexamples propagate through material assertion, execution\\nand evidence-use dependencies under [FOUNDATIONS Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse). Historical\\nevidence remains about its original subject. Reuse on a changed subject needs an\\nestablished applicability or preservation relation; rereading alone does not\\nestablish it. A new release does not invalidate a still-selected older release,\\nand a changed hash alone establishes neither semantic incompatibility nor\\ncontinued validity. Unknown impact holds the dependent assurance or widens\\nassessment; it does not require unrelated work to restart.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-07--change-evidence-and-reliance\",\"start_line\":980}],\"statements\":[\"Retain old-subject evidence and justified applicability across material change.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:759dcede800bb40bf1b35ef8393b00f2\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":995,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-07 — Change, evidence and reliance\\n\\nEach cross-boundary use binds the actual selected sources and material execution\\nbasis, including uncommitted bytes where relevant. A moving selection identifies\\nhow advancement is detected and which reliance must be reassessed. Git is one\\npossible carrier, not a mandatory identity system.\\n\\nChanges and new counterexamples propagate through material assertion, execution\\nand evidence-use dependencies under [FOUNDATIONS Change impact and evidence reuse](FOUNDATIONS.md#change-impact-and-evidence-reuse). Historical\\nevidence remains about its original subject. Reuse on a changed subject needs an\\nestablished applicability or preservation relation; rereading alone does not\\nestablish it. A new release does not invalidate a still-selected older release,\\nand a changed hash alone establishes neither semantic incompatibility nor\\ncontinued validity. Unknown impact holds the dependent assurance or widens\\nassessment; it does not require unrelated work to restart.\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-07--change-evidence-and-reliance\",\"start_line\":980}],\"statements\":[\"Use a changed hash or rereading alone to prove invalidity or equivalence.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3e3f03245d00d6080a6a206cef4a155e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3","key":29,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep unsupported adequacy/clean-room claims unresolved and use the declared re-entry.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:acc8c965a48d0a6498144ae726e9a1a5\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":963,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-05 — Context construction and clean-room conditions\\n\\nAn actor's selected context must satisfy both permission and adequacy for its\\nengagement. Permission covers the source information and permitted derivations,\\nnot only paths or filenames. The boundary identifies eligible source classes,\\nexports and tool outputs, material provenance, intended use, later acquisitions\\nand the effect of prior exposure. An allowed file location or a fresh summary\\ndoes not sanitize prohibited information.\\n\\nA target owner may authorize an export, but clean-room eligibility additionally\\nrequires that the engagement's information policy admits that export and its\\nprovenance. The actual delivered/acquired material must be recorded to the extent\\nrequired by the claim. An uncertain or prohibited exposure follows the declared\\nhold/re-entry rule; it cannot be repaired by deleting its receipt or relabeling\\nthe same actor fresh. Prior actor knowledge and external acquisition channels are\\npart of the declared limits.\\n\\nAdequacy retains the distinctions required for the task's decisions and\\ncontinuations, including unresolved obligations, result standing, currentness and\\nauthority. If the permitted material is insufficient, acquire an authorized\\nextension, narrow the task with the owner, use a suitable actor or return the\\nunresolved outcome. Permission is not evidence of sufficiency, and a budget is\\nnot permission to omit a deciding condition. This applies [FOUNDATIONS Observation sufficiency](FOUNDATIONS.md#assurance-relations)\\nand its scoped preservation law; it supplies no general optimal context selector (P1, P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions\",\"start_line\":939}],\"statement\":\"Permission alone cannot establish semantic sufficiency or exclude unknown prior/external exposure.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:a62977ad70d316938830d82d18f33f6d","key":30,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949