\"traversals\"],\"local_sorts\":[],\"type\":\"ref\"},\"min_items\":0,\"type\":\"array\"},\"subject\":{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"domain\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:reference-domain:declared\",\"external_kinds\":[],\"governing\":true,\"local_families\":[\"objects\",\"relations\",\"constraints\",\"latitude\"],\"local_sorts\":[],\"type\":\"ref\"},\"uncertainty\":{\"fields\":{\"grounding\":{\"items\":{\"fields\":{\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"path\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"quote\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"section\":{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"domain\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:reference-domain:declared\",\"external_kinds\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:external-kind:source-section\"],\"governing\":false,\"local_families\":[],\"local_sorts\":[],\"type\":\"ref\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"min_items\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"statement\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}},\"sorts\":{\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:sort:authored-concept\":{\"value\":{\"fields\":{\"conditions\":{\"items\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"min_items\":0,\"type\":\"array\"},\"definition\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"exceptions\":{\"items\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"min_items\":0,\"type\":\"array\"},\"grounding\":{\"items\":{\"fields\":{\"end_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"},\"path\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"quote\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"},\"section\":{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"domain\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:reference-domain:declared\",\"external_kinds\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:external-kind:source-section\"],\"governing\":false,\"local_families\":[],\"local_sorts\":[],\"type\":\"ref\"},\"start_line\":{\"type\":\"integer\"}},\"type\":\"object\"},\"min_items\":1,\"type\":\"array\"},\"label\":{\"min_length\":1,\"type\":\"string\"}},\"type\":\"object\"}}},\"stop_kinds\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:signature:compact-source-proposal-v1\",\"sha256\":\"ba18237c16ba9bed43b058c27b135a7bb2f19fd8d79ee0ac76b309df26ba3ee7\"}}","parentIdentity":"urn:stdo:3.0.2:composition-release:interpretation:1","parentRawSha256":"fc3114dd666218c387a64846b755a14979182f488de64ffff6a6d305a9698793","records":[{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"objects","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:e11c5f8f20036380d2948b6787deaaed","key":9,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:e11c5f8f20036380d2948b6787deaaed\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"sort\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:sort:authored-concept\",\"value\":{\"conditions\":[\"Within the release-profile scope and explicit qualifications in this source section.\"],\"definition\":\"RC channels discover the highest positive ordinal; stable channels resolve one exact stable cut. Both require a separately presented digest-bound adoption plan and refuse drift or ambiguous identity.\",\"exceptions\":[],\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":483,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"## 4. Selector and consumer adoption\\n\\nAn RC-profile version-line selector answers only (P6, P3):\\n\\n> Which highest-ordinal published immutable RC cut currently exists on\\n> this version line?\\n\\nIt never answers:\\n\\n> Which exact STDO cut governs this consumer?\\n\\nA Product Definition may retain `stdo://channels/<version>` as its\\ndiscovery selector, but its operative basis is the exact\\n`stdo://releases/v<version>-rc.<n>/` or stable\\n`stdo://releases/v<major>.<minor>.<patch>/` URI and installed-manifest digest,\\nthe installed release basis of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4. Moving the Git\\nversion-line selector does not update any consumer. Adoption is a separate\\nexplicit Product-Definition transition that resolves, presents, installs,\\nverifies and pins the selected immutable cut. RC resolution requires an\\nannotated selector with a distinct peeled commit; absence of a peeled\\nselector ref fails closed and cannot be interpreted as a lightweight\\nselector whose tag object is its commit (P6, P3, P5).\\n\\nFor an RC line, channel resolution enumerates the published RC tags for the selected\\nProject Release Namespace, including preserved unqualified historical cuts\\nduring a namespace transition, selects the greatest positive ordinal,\\nrequires that cut and the current selector to be annotated tags peeling to\\nthe same commit, and fails closed when the selector lags or points\\nelsewhere. Channel adoption also refuses a same-line target whose ordinal\\nis below the Product Definition's current exact basis. A consumer that\\nintentionally retains an older cut names that immutable RC URI and digest\\nexplicitly and uses exact-basis operations such as `sync`; it does not\\nexpress that choice through the latest-version channel (P5, P6).\\n\\nFor a stable line, channel resolution returns its verified stable-v1 cut\\nwithout ordinal comparison or a separate selector. A legacy bare selector is\\nnever admitted as a stable exact basis; an ambiguous profile is refused. The\\nsame digest-bound adoption operation applies to either profile (P3, P5, P6).\\n\\nPresentation and mutation are separate invocations. The read-only plan,\\nthe Adoption Plan of PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4, binds the current Product\\nDefinition bytes and basis to the target immutable cut, annotated tag\\nobject, peeled commit, tree and installed-manifest digest, then emits a\\ndeterministic plan digest. Mutation requires that exact digest as the\\noperator's acceptance and re-derives it before changing any Product\\nDefinition. Selector, target, manifest or definition drift invalidates the\\nacceptance. A fleet uses the same law with one aggregate digest over all\\nexact per-definition plans. Planning inside a mutating invocation is not\\nexternal presentation and cannot authorise itself. The plan's hashing rule\\nand the manager's command boundaries are PRODUCT_DEFINITION §4 (P6, P3).\\n\\nThis split lets operators refer to `v<version>` for the latest published\\nRC without repeatedly incrementing the version line, while every governed\\nproject retains reproducible exact-cut authority and changes only through\\nexplicit adoption (P2, P3, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#4-selector-and-consumer-adoption\",\"start_line\":428}],\"label\":\"Profile-specific discovery and explicit adoption\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"constraints","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:17709a533f0a1e16052a4cd40e74afe8","key":22,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:e11c5f8f20036380d2948b6787deaaed\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"u