limits.\\n\\nAdequacy retains the distinctions required for the task's decisions and\\ncontinuations, including unresolved obligations, result standing, currentness and\\nauthority. If the permitted material is insufficient, acquire an authorized\\nextension, narrow the task with the owner, use a suitable actor or return the\\nunresolved outcome. Permission is not evidence of sufficiency, and a budget is\\nnot permission to omit a deciding condition. This applies [FOUNDATIONS Observation sufficiency](FOUNDATIONS.md#assurance-relations)\\nand its scoped preservation law; it supplies no general optimal context selector (P1, P2, P6).\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3","key":29,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep unsupported adequacy/clean-room claims unresolved and use the declared re-entry.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:acc8c965a48d0a6498144ae726e9a1a5\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":963,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-05 — Context construction and clean-room conditions\\n\\nAn actor's selected context must satisfy both permission and adequacy for its\\nengagement. Permission covers the source information and permitted derivations,\\nnot only paths or filenames. The boundary identifies eligible source classes,\\nexports and tool outputs, material provenance, intended use, later acquisitions\\nand the effect of prior exposure. An allowed file location or a fresh summary\\ndoes not sanitize prohibited information.\\n\\nA target owner may authorize an export, but clean-room eligibility additionally\\nrequires that the engagement's information policy admits that export and its\\nprovenance. The actual delivered/acquired material must be recorded to the extent\\nrequired by the claim. An uncertain or prohibited exposure follows the declared\\nhold/re-entry rule; it cannot be repaired by deleting its receipt or relabeling\\nthe same actor fresh. Prior actor knowledge and external acquisition channels are\\npart of the declared limits.\\n\\nAdequacy retains the distinctions required for the task's decisions and\\ncontinuations, including unresolved obligations, result standing, currentness and\\nauthority. If the permitted material is insufficient, acquire an authorized\\nextension, narrow the task with the owner, use a suitable actor or return the\\nunresolved outcome. Permission is not evidence of sufficiency, and a budget is\\nnot permission to omit a deciding condition. This applies [FOUNDATIONS Observation sufficiency](FOUNDATIONS.md#assurance-relations)\\nand its scoped preservation law; it supplies no general optimal context selector (P1, P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions\",\"start_line\":939}],\"statement\":\"Permission alone cannot establish semantic sufficiency or exclude unknown prior/external exposure.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"seeds":[29],"unresolved":[{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3","key":29,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Keep unsupported adequacy/clean-room claims unresolved and use the declared re-entry.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:9f379db2ef9a8451a57bc145d36d9db3\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:acc8c965a48d0a6498144ae726e9a1a5\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":963,\"path\":\"standards/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md\",\"quote\":\"### PC-05 — Context construction and clean-room conditions\\n\\nAn actor's selected context must satisfy both permission and adequacy for its\\nengagement. Permission covers the source information and permitted derivations,\\nnot only paths or filenames. The boundary identifies eligible source classes,\\nexports and tool outputs, material provenance, intended use, later acquisitions\\nand the effect of prior exposure. An allowed file location or a fresh summary\\ndoes not sanitize prohibited information.\\n\\nA target owner may authorize an export, but clean-room eligibility additionally\\nrequires that the engagement's information policy admits that export and its\\nprovenance. The actual delivered/acquired material must be recorded to the extent\\nrequired by the claim. An uncertain or prohibited exposure follows the declared\\nhold/re-entry rule; it cannot be repaired by deleting its receipt or relabeling\\nthe same actor fresh. Prior actor knowledge and external acquisition channels are\\npart of the declared limits.\\n\\nAdequacy retains the distinctions required for the task's decisions and\\ncontinuations, including unresolved obligations, result standing, currentness and\\nauthority. If the permitted material is insufficient, acquire an authorized\\nextension, narrow the task with the owner, use a suitable actor or return the\\nunresolved outcome. Permission is not evidence of sufficiency, and a budget is\\nnot permission to omit a deciding condition. This applies [FOUNDATIONS Observation sufficiency](FOUNDATIONS.md#assurance-relations)\\nand its scoped preservation law; it supplies no general optimal context selector (P1, P2, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions\",\"start_line\":939}],\"statement\":\"Permission alone cannot establish semantic sufficiency or exclude unknown prior/external exposure.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}]},"underbudgetRefusal":"insufficient record budget; required closure is not truncated"},{"budget":11,"projection":{"excluded":[0,1,3,5,7,8,9,10,13,14,16,18,20,21,22,23,24,25,26,28,31],"excludedResiduals":[{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9","key":31,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the exact evidence and owner verdicts for each semantic or acceptance claim.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6cc92570e9e1d4cc0b93ea894305e162\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Immutable stable publication\\n\\nStable publication applies the same scope, source reconciliation, proportionate\\nchecks, exact carrier, subtree and inventory obligations as RC publication.\\nIt instead creates one stable-v1 annotated tag and any explicitly selected\\nrelease branch, with no RC branch or separate selector. Before publication,\\nverify the fresh-line conditions of [Stable cuts](#stable-cuts), bind remote\\nabsence for the immutable tag and bind every mutable destination's expected\\nobject. Publish the selected refs atomically where supported; a changed\\nexpectation stops publication for reconciliation. Read back the remote tag\\nobject, commit, subtree and declared assets. The release is publicly classified\\nas a normal published release; release-host flags do not replace exact identity\\nor qualification evidence (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#immutable-stable-publication\",\"start_line\":361}],\"statement\":\"A stable naming and discovery profile alone does not establish stronger semantic qualification.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"external":[{"identity":"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record","payload":"{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"evidence_identity\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:evidence:explicit-generation-signature\",\"external_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record\",\"external_target_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:external-kind:source-section\",\"reference_domain\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:reference-domain:declared\",\"resolution_basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"resolved_target_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-03--the-edges-contract-and-authority-record\"}"},{"identity":"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions","payload":"{\"basis_relation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis-relation:exact\",\"evidence_identity\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:evidence:explicit-generation-signature\",\"external_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions\",\"external_target_kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:external-kind:source-section\",\"reference_domain\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:reference-domain:declared\",\"resolution_basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"resolved_target_identity\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-05--context-construction-and-clean-room-conditions\"}"},{"identity":"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/PRODUCT_DEFINITION.md#pc-07--change-evide