 is absent (`null`), and resolution\\nmust verify the stable profile and complete identity. That channel route\\ncreates neither another tag nor mutable alias semantics. Consumer adoption\\nstill follows §4 (P3, P6).\\n\\nA published stable tag never moves. Any change to its qualifying bytes\\nrequires a new version and a new immutable cut, not an RC added to the\\nalready stable line. Historical RC lines keep their selector semantics,\\nrefs, objects, peels and URIs; this profile neither finalises nor renames\\nthem. An RC-labelled published release remains a proper release (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#stable-cuts\",\"start_line\":206}],\"statement\":\"The `stable-v1` profile publishes an immutable release directly as\\n`refs/tags/<project>/v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`. Each numeric component is a\\nnonnegative decimal integer, with no leading zero except the single digit\\n`0`. The tag is annotated, targets a commit and contains exactly one\\nstandalone annotation line (P3):\\n\\n```text\\nSTDO-Release-Profile: stable-v1\\n```\\n\\nIts exact release declaration names the same stable cut, declared payload,\\nsource selection and predecessor. The installed manifest records\\n`release.profile = \\\"stable-v1\\\"` alongside the complete identity of\\n[Project-subtree release identity](#project-subtree-release-identity).\\nAn RC manifest retains its prior shape; adding stable support must not\\nchange the canonical bytes of a historical release manifest (P3, P4b).\\n\\nThe stable coordinate is available only on a fresh version line with no\\nsame-version RC tag in either the historical or project-qualified namespace\\nand no historical unqualified bare-version tag. The stable tag itself is\\ncreate-only. A same-line collision or a missing, duplicated or different\\nprofile marker refuses stable acquisition; bare spelling or annotation alone\\ncannot turn an RC selector into an immutable cut (P3, P5).\\n\\nThere is no separate version-line selector or RC branch for this profile.\\nA channel `stdo://channels/<major>.<minor>.<patch>` may discover that exact\\nimmutable stable tag; its cut ordinal is absent (`null`), and resolution\\nmust verify the stable profile and complete identity. That channel route\\ncreates neither another tag nor mutable alias semantics. Consumer adoption\\nstill follows §4 (P3, P6).\\n\\nA published stable tag never moves. Any change to its qualifying bytes\\nrequires a new version and a new immutable cut, not an RC added to the\\nalready stable line. Historical RC lines keep their selector semantics,\\nrefs, objects, peels and URIs; this profile neither finalises nor renames\\nthem. An RC-labelled published release remains a proper release (P3, P4b).\",\"uncertainty\":\"\"},\"refusal\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:stop:no-execution-or-acceptance\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"latitude","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6a12fb58908bea23f5b12f8cdb512d7e","key":28,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"allowed_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":244,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Stable cuts\\n\\nThe `stable-v1` profile publishes an immutable release directly as\\n`refs/tags/<project>/v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`. Each numeric component is a\\nnonnegative decimal integer, with no leading zero except the single digit\\n`0`. The tag is annotated, targets a commit and contains exactly one\\nstandalone annotation line (P3):\\n\\n```text\\nSTDO-Release-Profile: stable-v1\\n```\\n\\nIts exact release declaration names the same stable cut, declared payload,\\nsource selection and predecessor. The installed manifest records\\n`release.profile = \\\"stable-v1\\\"` alongside the complete identity of\\n[Project-subtree release identity](#project-subtree-release-identity).\\nAn RC manifest retains its prior shape; adding stable support must not\\nchange the canonical bytes of a historical release manifest (P3, P4b).\\n\\nThe stable coordinate is available only on a fresh version line with no\\nsame-version RC tag in either the historical or project-qualified namespace\\nand no historical unqualified bare-version tag. The stable tag itself is\\ncreate-only. A same-line collision or a missing, duplicated or different\\nprofile marker refuses stable acquisition; bare spelling or annotation alone\\ncannot turn an RC selector into an immutable cut (P3, P5).\\n\\nThere is no separate version-line selector or RC branch for this profile.\\nA channel `stdo://channels/<major>.<minor>.<patch>` may discover that exact\\nimmutable stable tag; its cut ordinal is absent (`null`), and resolution\\nmust verify the stable profile and complete identity. That channel route\\ncreates neither another tag nor mutable alias semantics. Consumer adoption\\nstill follows §4 (P3, P6).\\n\\nA published stable tag never moves. Any change to its qualifying bytes\\nrequires a new version and a new immutable cut, not an RC added to the\\nalready stable line. Historical RC lines keep their selector semantics,\\nrefs, objects, peels and URIs; this profile neither finalises nor renames\\nthem. An RC-labelled published release remains a proper release (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#stable-cuts\",\"start_line\":206}],\"statements\":[\"Select a directly published stable cut on a fresh version line under stable-v1; preserved RC lines remain proper releases under their existing profile.\"]},\"applies_to\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6cc92570e9e1d4cc0b93ea894305e162\"],\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"forbidden_variation\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":244,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Stable cuts\\n\\nThe `stable-v1` profile publishes an immutable release directly as\\n`refs/tags/<project>/v<major>.<minor>.<patch>`. Each numeric component is a\\nnonnegative decimal integer, with no leading zero except the single digit\\n`0`. The tag is annotated, targets a commit and contains exactly one\\nstandalone annotation line (P3):\\n\\n```text\\nSTDO-Release-Profile: stable-v1\\n```\\n\\nIts exact release declaration names the same stable cut, declared payload,\\nsource selection and predecessor. The installed manifest records\\n`release.profile = \\\"stable-v1\\\"` alongside the complete identity of\\n[Project-subtree release identity](#project-subtree-release-identity).\\nAn RC manifest retains its prior shape; adding stable support must not\\nchange the canonical bytes of a historical release manifest (P3, P4b).\\n\\nThe stable coordinate is available only on a fresh version line with no\\nsame-version RC tag in either the historical or project-qualified namespace\\nand no historical unqualified bare-version tag. The stable tag itself is\\ncreate-only. A same-line collision or a missing, duplicated or different\\nprofile marker refuses stable acquisition; bare spelling or annotation alone\\ncannot turn an RC selector into an immutable cut (P3, P5).\\n\\nThere is no separate version-line selector or RC branch for this profile.\\nA channel `stdo://channels/<major>.<minor>.<patch>` may discover that exact\\nimmutable stable tag; its cut ordinal is absent (`null`), and resolution\\nmust verify the stable profile and complete identity. That channel route\\ncreates neither another tag nor mutable alias semantics. Consumer adoption\\nstill follows §4 (P3, P6).\\n\\nA published stable tag never moves. Any change to its qualifying bytes\\nrequires a new version and a new immutable cut, not an RC added to the\\nalready stable line. Historical RC lines keep their selector semantics,\\nrefs, objects, peels and URIs; this profile neither finalises nor renames\\nthem. An RC-labelled published release remains a proper release (P3, P4b).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#stable-cuts\",\"start_line\":206}],\"statements\":[\"Reinterpret a legacy bare RC selector as an immutable stable cut.\",\"Move a published stable tag or add a repair RC to its already stable line.\"]},\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6a12fb58908bea23f5b12f8cdb512d7e\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"},{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9","key":31,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the exact evidence and owner verdicts for each semantic or acceptance claim.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6cc92570e9e1d4cc0b93ea894305e162\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Immutable stable publication\\n\\nStable publication applies the same scope, source reconciliation, proportionate\\nchecks, exact carrier, subtree and inventory obligations as RC publication.\\nIt instead creates one stable-v1 annotated tag and any explicitly selected\\nrelease branch, with no RC branch or separate selector. Before publication,\\nverify the fresh-line conditions of [Stable cuts](#stable-cuts), bind remote\\nabsence for the immutable tag and bind every mutable destination's expected\\nobject. Publish the selected refs atomically where supported; a changed\\nexpectation stops publication for reconciliation. Read back the remote tag\\nobject, commit, subtree and declared assets. The release is publicly classified\\nas a normal published release; release-host flags do not replace exact identity\\nor qualification evidence (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#immutable-stable-publication\",\"start_line\":361}],\"statement\":\"A stable naming and discovery profile alone does not establish stronger semantic qualification.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}],"seeds":[31],"unresolved":[{"basis":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis","context":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal","family":"residuals","identity":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9","key":31,"owner":"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author","payload":"{\"basis\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:basis\",\"consequence\":\"Retain the exact evidence and owner verdicts for each semantic or acceptance claim.\",\"context\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:context:source-first-proposal\",\"id\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:3b3041db69d216ff76f8fe4e6d41e9b9\",\"invalidation\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:invalidation:source-or-interpretation-change\",\"kind\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:residual-kind:authored-uncertainty\",\"owner\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:actor:f-p-author\",\"re_entry\":[],\"scope\":[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"],\"subject\":\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:record:6cc92570e9e1d4cc0b93ea894305e162\",\"uncertainty\":{\"grounding\":[{\"end_line\":374,\"path\":\"standards/RELEASE.md\",\"quote\":\"### Immutable stable publication\\n\\nStable publication applies the same scope, source reconciliation, proportionate\\nchecks, exact carrier, subtree and inventory obligations as RC publication.\\nIt instead creates one stable-v1 annotated tag and any explicitly selected\\nrelease branch, with no RC branch or separate selector. Before publication,\\nverify the fresh-line conditions of [Stable cuts](#stable-cuts), bind remote\\nabsence for the immutable tag and bind every mutable destination's expected\\nobject. Publish the selected refs atomically where supported; a changed\\nexpectation stops publication for reconciliation. Read back the remote tag\\nobject, commit, subtree and declared assets. The release is publicly classified\\nas a normal published release; release-host flags do not replace exact identity\\nor qualification evidence (P3, P5, P6).\",\"section\":\"repo://stdo-v3.0.2-source/RELEASE.md#immutable-stable-publication\",\"start_line\":361}],\"statement\":\"A stable naming and discovery profile alone does not establish stronger semantic qualification.\"}}","scope":"[\"urn:a-c:generation:630ce49ea536c4b3949b529c:scope:source-corpus\"]"}]},"underbudgetRefusal":"insufficient record budget; required closure is not truncated"}],"toy":[{"budget":1,"proje